  "Number": 15,
  "Question": "A sale ad read: “Buy three tires at the regular price and get the fourth tire for \\(\\$3.\\)” Sam paid \\(\\$240\\) for a set of four tires at the sale. What was the regular price of one tire?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$59.25\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$60\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$70\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$79\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$80\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The fourth tire cost only \\(3\\) dollars. Removing that charge leaves the cost of the three regularly priced tires:\n\\[\n240-3=237\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nThose three tires have the same regular price, so divide their total cost equally among them:\n\\[\n237\\div3=79\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nThe regular price of one tire was \\(\\$79\\), choice D.",
